 {"attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": null, "blocks": [], "capability_tags": ["landlock", "egress", "wrapper"], "ci_result": null, "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-10-20T01:52:35+00:00", "created_by": null, "depends_on": [], "evidence": null, "id": "TJ-DF-050", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "Dogfood 2026-10-19 run 20 (first real use of the TJ-DF-046/047 fix, HEAD 29ae69f). The plain-allow half of the new degrade contract works; the auto-sandbox (modify) half does not, and its failure is unattributed.\n\nWHAT THE SHIPPED CONTRACT SAYS: README.md:77 \u2014 \"with the net tier opted in, a payload is never silently left with network egress unchanged \u2014 every non-attach outcome prints `terminal-jail: WARNING: Landlock network (egress) tier not applied (<cause>)` naming why (loader missing, unreadable under the launch, uid-mapped launch, ABI < 4, unproven enforcement, refused allowlist), on the plain-allow path exactly as on the auto-sandbox path (TJ-DF-046/047).\"\n\nFRESH INSTALL USED (dev host, HEAD 29ae69f, `/tmp/df-tj-1019/prefix`, rules dir pinned via TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_USER_RULES_DIR):\n\nLEG D \u2014 modify path, net loader unreadable (the defect):\n  $ chmod 000 /tmp/df-tj-1019/lib/terminal-jail/landlock-net-loader.py\n  $ TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1 /tmp/df-tj-1019/prefix/terminal-jail /usr/bin/python3 /tmp/df-tj-1019/payload.py 9999\n  {\"event\":\"verdict\",\"action\":\"modify\",\"rule_id\":\"auto-script\",\"layer\":\"yaml\",\u2026}\n  [terminal-jail] Modified: '/usr/bin/python3' '/tmp/df-tj-1019/payl... \u2192 sandboxed\n  terminal-jail: WARNING: Landlock filesystem tier not applied (\u2026)          <- fs tier only\n  python3: can't open file '/tmp/df-tj-1019/lib/terminal-jail/landlock-net-loader.py': [Errno 13] Permission denied\n  rc=2   ^ the payload NEVER ran, and NO named-cause egress line was printed \u2014 the user sees a raw Python error and a failed command\n\nLEG J \u2014 identical host state, plain-allow shape (the fixed path, for contrast):\n  $ chmod 000 /tmp/df-tj-1019/lib/terminal-jail/landlock-net-loader.py\n  $ TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1 /tmp/df-tj-1019/prefix/terminal-jail /usr/bin/python3 -c '<connect 9999 code>'\n  terminal-jail: WARNING: Landlock network (egress) tier not applied (the payload cannot read /tmp/df-tj-1019/prefix/../lib/terminal-jail/landlock-net-loader.py in the launch that would run it); commands run with network egress unchanged \u2014 \u2026\n  CONNECTED ok data=b'pong\\n'   (payload ran unchanged, cause named \u2014 correct)\n  (the same leg is reproduced on a fresh bunker box: HOME-installed tree, cause worded \"landlock-net-loader.py is not reachable by the launch's payload uid (a parent \u2026 lacks o+x \u2014 e.g. a 0700/0750 home)\")\n\nMECHANISM (two attach paths, two different checks):\n  - plain-allow path: standalone/terminal-jail:1046-1068 `_tj_egress_tier_decide` probes readability UNDER the launch it is about to run (`\"$@\" test -r \"$LANDLOCK_NET_LOADER\"`) and calls `_tj_egress_degrade` with the cause on every non-attach outcome \u2014 this is the half TJ-DF-046/047 fixed.\n  - modify path: the tail is composed INSIDE the engine before the wrapper ever sees it \u2014 plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/decider.py:76 `_LANDLOCK_NET_TAIL = landlock_net_sandbox_prefix()` spliced by `_wrap_payload` (:79), whose reachability gate is plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/landlock_net.py:727 `if not _world_traversable(loader)` \u2014 and `_world_traversable` (def plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/landlock.py:1201) walks ONLY the ancestor directories' `S_IXOTH`, never the loader file's own read bits. A loader that is path-traversable but unreadable by the payload uid therefore passes, gets spliced into the rewrite, and standalone/terminal-jail:1271+ execs the already-composed rewrite with no reachability preflight of its own.\n\nWHY THE STATE IS REACHABLE, NOT A LAB CURIOSITY: any install whose loader keeps a path the payload uid can traverse but loses the file's read bit \u2014 a loader owned by another uid with 0600 (split-user or root-owned install run by a user), a tightened umask/ACL, a packaging step that drops modes. The uid-mapped arm is already handled (landlock_net.py:1058 branch, `--here` semantics), so this is the remaining hole in the same contract.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: in `sandbox_prefix()` test the loader's OWN readability for the launch uid (e.g. `os.access`/mode & 0o444 after the traversal walk) in addition to `_world_traversable`, and on failure return the empty tail + the existing `_degrade(...)` wording, so the payload runs unchanged with one named-cause line \u2014 the same posture the fs tier uses. Keep the plain-allow path's wording as-is (it is already correct).\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA: with the net tier enabled and the net loader chmod 000, an auto-sandbox-shaped command (a script payload) still RUNS (rc from the payload, not 2) and stderr carries exactly one `WARNING: Landlock network (egress) tier not applied (<cause>)` line naming the unreadable loader; no raw `python3: can't open file \u2026 [Errno 13]` reaches the user.", "status": "pending", "title": "[P2] auto-sandbox (modify) path splices the net loader without a readability preflight: a loader unreadable by the payload uid passes _world_traversable (ancestor o+x only), so the rewrite dies with a raw python Errno 13 + rc=2 and NO named-cause line, while the plain-allow path degrades loudly on the identical state", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T01:52:35+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "ff09c9c6a23200dd60a8b03bc047efc953119b7169a52ed20d21f6cdca34e9fe"}}
 {"id": "TJ-DF-051", "title": "[P2] composed-mode launch reports the egress tier BOTH ways in one run: the engine gate prints 'not reachable ... lacks o+x' and the composed path then attaches it ('egress: enforced by terminal-jail' + 'kernel egress tier APPLIED', connect denied EACCES) - reproduced on a fresh 0750-home bunker box in two layouts", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 3, "capability_tags": ["landlock", "egress", "composed-mode", "reporting"], "attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": null, "blocks": [], "depends_on": [], "ci_result": null, "created_at": "2026-10-20T02:05:15+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T02:05:15+00:00", "created_by": "terminal-jail-dogfood", "evidence": null, "detail": null, "reasoning": "Dogfood 2026-10-20 run 21 (second angle on the TJ-DF-046/047 landing; sibling run 20 filed TJ-DF-049/050 + INT-CI-009). Angle: the COMPOSED-mode launch shape on a FRESH 0750-home box + the install containment-ceiling arms \u2014 surfaces neither run 17/19/20 drove.\n\nWHAT ONE LAUNCH PRINTS (verbatim, fresh bunker agent e7f7ce38 on bunker-mvp, kernel 6.8.0-142, Landlock ABI 4, HOME mode 0750, install via ./install.sh):\n\n  $ TERMINAL_JAIL_COMPOSED=on TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1 terminal-jail /usr/bin/python3 -c '<connect 443 then 19099>'\n  terminal-jail: WARNING: Landlock filesystem tier not applied (layout refused); ...\n  terminal-jail: WARNING: Landlock network (egress) tier not applied (landlock-net-loader.py is not reachable by the launch's payload uid (a parent of /home/bunker-e7f7ce38/.local/lib/terminal-jail/landlock-net-loader.py lacks o+x - e.g. a 0700/0750 home)); commands run with network egress unchanged ...\n  {\"event\":\"verdict\",\"action\":\"allow\",\"rule_id\":null,\"layer\":\"engine\", ...}\n  terminal-jail: COMPOSED MODE - running without an inner namespace\n  terminal-jail: composed layers - egress: enforced by terminal-jail (kernel Landlock TCP-connect allowlist; this tier needs no namespace)\n  terminal-jail: landlock-net: kernel egress tier APPLIED - TCP connect() restricted to ports [22, 53, 80, 443]; ...\n  RESULT port=443 CONNECTED\n  RESULT port=19099 errno=13 Permission denied      <- the kernel really is denying\n  PROBE-DONE   (rc=0)\n\nSo ONE launch states the egress tier is NOT applied and then that it IS applied and enforced. The applied half is the truth (the payload's connect() to the non-allowlisted port returns EACCES/errno 13; with TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=0 the same payload CONNECTs) \u2014 the \"not applied\" line is a FALSE NEGATIVE that a user cannot tell apart from a real degrade.\n\nREPRODUCED TWICE on that box, two layouts: (a) the install.sh layout (~/.local/lib/terminal-jail), (b) a copy the user owns (~/n750/lib/terminal-jail, dir mode 0750). The owner CAN read the loader in both (os.access R_OK = True, open() ok, head -c 40 rc=0) \u2014 so \"not reachable by the launch's payload uid\" is wrong for a composed launch, which creates no inner namespace and runs the payload as the OWNER.\n\nMECHANISM (two independent attach decisions, two different payload-uid assumptions):\n  - the ENGINE gate: plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/landlock_net.py:727-731 -> _world_traversable() (plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/landlock.py:1201) demands S_IXOTH on EVERY ancestor, documented as \"a mapping-less rewrite runs its payload as nobody (65534)\"; the twin fs gate at landlock.py:1312. On a 0750 home this returns False and emits the WARNING above.\n  - the COMPOSED attach: standalone/terminal-jail _tj_egress_tier_decide --here (the `--here` branch is documented \"probes in THIS context, for the composed launch, where the payload gets no inner namespace and no uid mapping\") -> its `test -r` passes (owner) -> TJ_EGRESS_TIER_ATTACH=1 -> loader runs -> \"kernel egress tier APPLIED\".\n  In composed mode BOTH decisions run for the same launch and disagree, and the composed-mode layer report (\"egress: enforced by terminal-jail\") lands in between.\n\nSAME ROOT, SECOND SYMPTOM (duplicate, not contradictory): with an invalid allowlist token, ONE launch prints the tier refusal twice \u2014 a plain-allow/modify launch with TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET_ALLOW=bogus-port prints first \"WARNING: Landlock network (egress) tier not applied (probe crash: invalid TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET_ALLOW token 'bogus-port' - expected a port (1-65535) or one of ['dns','domain','http','https','ssh']; refusing to apply a misparsed allowlist); ...\" and then a second \"... tier not applied (invalid allowlist token 'bogus-port'); ...\" from the engine's own compose path. One condition, two lines, two wordings \u2014 the same two-surface reporting.\n\nIMPACT: the tier's own degrade contract (README.md:77, TJ-DF-046/047) says every non-attach outcome is stated once and loudly so a payload is never silently left CONNECTED. In composed mode on a standard 0750-home box the operator is told the tier is off while it is on; the transcript cannot be used as containment evidence, and a scripted check that greps for \"not applied\" (or for \"APPLIED\") gets whichever answer it looks for.\n\nWHAT IS **NOT** BROKEN (tested for, so nobody chases it): the plain-allow path on the CONTROL host (HOME 0751) applies the tier cleanly; a 0750 parent on the control host does NOT by itself produce the WARNING (plain bwrap launch applies, no degrade line) \u2014 the trigger is the composed/userns-less shape, not the directory mode alone; the missing/unreadable-loader degrade arms print exactly one named-cause line each on the plain-allow path and the payload still runs (re-verified this run, checklist control host + fresh box); the fresh box's plain (non-composed) launch refuses to run at all with rc=2 \"namespace creation failed (unshare exit 1)\" plus the CAP_SYS_ADMIN/composed-mode guidance \u2014 honest, environment-caused (the bunker agent is a container).\n\nFIX DIRECTION: make the attach decision for a composed launch come from the payload uid it will actually have. Either (a) skip the nobody-assuming _world_traversable gate on the composed path (the `--here` semantics standalone/terminal-jail already implements) so the engine does not emit a degrade line for a launch it does not own, or (b) let the composed attach OVERRIDE the engine's line when it attaches, or (c) pass the launch's real uid into the gate. Same change removes the duplicate bad-allowlist pair (one condition -> one line).\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:\n 1. On a 0750-home box with TERMINAL_JAIL_COMPOSED=on TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1, one launch never prints both \"Landlock network (egress) tier not applied\" and \"kernel egress tier APPLIED\"; either the tier attaches (APPLIED only, or no degrade line) or it does not attach (exactly one named-cause WARNING).\n 2. An invalid TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET_ALLOW token produces exactly ONE degrade line naming the token.\n 3. A regression test drives the composed launch shape with a 0750 ancestor and asserts \"not applied\" and \"APPLIED\" never co-occur in one launch's stderr.\n\nEVIDENCE THIS RUN: control host legs /tmp/df-tj-1020/ladder2.sh + ladder4.sh + ladder5.sh + ab_0750.sh logs; fresh box /home/bunker-e7f7ce38/{la,lb,lc}.err (agent e7f7ce38, destroyed; archive on bunker-mvp), remote scripts /tmp/df-tj-1020/remote_leg.sh, remote_diag.sh, remote_diag2.sh, remote_layout.sh; integration report docs/dogfood/2026-10-20-composed-mode-egress-reporting.md; install leg hand-walked because bunker-qa.sh is dead fleet-wide (INT-CI-009)."}
 {"id": "TJ-DF-052", "title": "[P3] the composed+egress regression cell cannot fail: plugin/test_tjdf046_egress_allow_path.py asserts 'egress: enforced by terminal-jail' OR 'Landlock network (egress) tier not applied' (or), so the exact contradictory pair filed as TJ-DF-051 satisfies it - and the cell pytest.skips on any host that can create inner namespaces", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "capability_tags": ["tests", "landlock", "egress", "composed-mode"], "attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": null, "blocks": [], "depends_on": [], "ci_result": null, "created_at": "2026-10-20T02:13:56+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T02:13:56+00:00", "created_by": "terminal-jail-dogfood", "evidence": null, "detail": null, "reasoning": "Dogfood 2026-10-20 run 21b (same tick, second angle; run 21 is the sibling \u2014 it filed TJ-DF-051). Angle: the documented audit tooling. Driving the batteries as a maintainer would led to the question \"why is the suite green while TJ-DF-051 is live?\", and the answer is a regression cell that cannot fail.\n\nTHE CELL (plugin/test_tjdf046_egress_allow_path.py, the composed arm of the TJ-DF-046 fix):\n\n    env[\"TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET\"] = \"1\"\n    env[\"TERMINAL_JAIL_COMPOSED\"] = \"on\"\n    result = _run_cli(\"echo\", \"tj-df-046-composed\", env=env)\n    if \"COMPOSED MODE\" not in result.stderr:\n        pytest.skip(\"this host creates inner namespaces, so composed mode is unreachable here\")\n    assert \"tj-df-046-composed\" in result.stdout, result.stderr\n    assert \"egress: enforced by terminal-jail\" in result.stderr or (\n        \"Landlock network (egress) tier not applied\" in result.stderr\n    ), result.stderr\n\nDEFECT 1 - the assertion accepts EITHER half of the contradictory pair. TJ-DF-051's launch prints \"Landlock network (egress) tier not applied (\u2026 lacks o+x \u2026)\" AND \"composed layers \u2014 egress: enforced by terminal-jail\" AND \"kernel egress tier APPLIED\" in ONE run; the `or` is satisfied by the second (or the first) alone, so the cell PASSES on the exact state the row files. It does still catch the ORIGINAL TJ-DF-046 class (silent: neither line) \u2014 which is why it was written that way \u2014 but it is structurally incapable of failing on the double report. A regression cell for a \"never contradict itself\" contract has to assert the ABSENCE of the other half, not the presence of one.\n\nDEFECT 2 - the cell skips exactly where it cannot help, and never exercises the failing shape. (a) The skip fires whenever the host CAN create an inner namespace (composed mode is then unreachable) - verified on the control host this run: TERMINAL_JAIL_COMPOSED=on took the normal bwrap launch, no \"COMPOSED MODE\" line, so the cell skips there and reads as green in the suite summary. (b) It only ever runs the loader from the CHECKOUT (standalone/landlock-net-loader.py under the repo), whose ancestors are world-traversable on the dev host (/home/kara = 0751), so the engine's _world_traversable gate passes and the false degrade line cannot appear in the covered shape. The shape that fails (loader behind a 0750 ancestor \u2014 the fleet's own bunker agents and Ubuntu's default user home; or the installer's ~/.local/lib tree under a 0750 $HOME) is not covered by any cell.\n\nIMPACT: the composed + egress-tier contract is a NEW surface (7971495/9a5a642, 2026-10-18) whose only regression coverage is a cell that skips on namespace-capable hosts and cannot fail where it runs. TJ-DF-051 landed green through a full 2027-pass suite for exactly this reason.\n\nFIX DIRECTION:\n 1. Assert the PAIR cannot co-occur: when \"egress: enforced by terminal-jail\" is present, assert the count of \"Landlock network (egress) tier not applied\" is 0 (and vice versa); keep the \"neither line\" failure for the silent class.\n 2. Add a cell that puts the loader behind a 0750 ancestor (a tmp dir with mode 750 holding a copied landlock-net-loader.py + its plugin tree, driven via TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET_LOADER / a scratch install) and, with TERMINAL_JAIL_COMPOSED=on, asserts exactly one verdict line; on a namespace-capable host assert the same through the plain path.\n 3. Make the skip visible as a skip, never as a pass: a `pytest.skip` inside a cell that also has a meaningful assertion reads as green coverage in the suite summary; prefer an explicit \"SKIPPED (host creates namespaces)\" print plus a separate host-independent cell that always exercises the composed-composition decision (the decision itself is testable without a container).\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:\n - With the net loader behind a 0750 ancestor and TERMINAL_JAIL_COMPOSED=on, the test fails BEFORE the TJ-DF-051 fix (co-occurrence detected) and passes after it, on a host that can create inner namespaces.\n - A run in which the composed arm skips is distinguishable from one in which it asserted (skip reported, not counted as coverage).\n - No cell in plugin/test_tjdf046_egress_allow_path.py or plugin/test_tjdf047_plain_allow_degrade.py asserts a one-of-two string as proof of a mutually-exclusive contract.\n\nEVIDENCE THIS RUN: control host legs (T3/T5 composed runs took the plain bwrap path with no COMPOSED MODE line -> the cell's skip condition), /tmp/df-tj-1020/ab0750.log (750 vs 755 parent A/B), the fresh-box transcripts quoted in TJ-DF-051 (agent e7f7ce38, both lines in one launch), and this row's grep of the suite: `grep -n COMPOSED plugin/test_tjdf046_egress_allow_path.py` -> lines 595-605 only; no cell in the repo pairs a 0750 ancestor with the composed arm."}
+{"id": "INT-CI-010", "title": "[P2] CI lint lane red on main: `ruff format --check .` rejected the python fence in docs/dogfood/2026-10-20-composed-mode-egress-reporting.md (introduced by dogfood run 21, 016adc1) \u2014 fixed in 723ddd6", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "created_at": "2026-10-20T03:19:37Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T03:19:37Z", "created_by": "foreman tick terminal-jail-foreman-2026-10-20-03-04-28 (CI-health intake)", "capability_tags": ["ci", "docs", "harness"], "complexity": 2, "attempts": 1, "blocks": [], "blocked_reason": null, "depends_on": [], "ci_result": "run 39363383191 @ 723ddd6 \u2014 all 6 jobs success", "reasoning": "CI-health check at tick start: `gh run list --repo terminal-jail/terminal-jail --limit 5` showed 5 consecutive failures on main (aa19097, 928ff93, 016adc1, 5429bdb, 1f830c5). Two lanes were red. Lint lane (this row): `ruff format --check .` fails because ruff formats python fences inside markdown, and the run-21 dogfood report quotes the composed arm of plugin/test_tjdf046_egress_allow_path.py with the long `pytest.skip(...)` call on one line. Reproduced locally at 1f830c5: `1 file would be reformatted, 152 files already formatted`, naming docs/dogfood/2026-10-20-composed-mode-egress-reporting.md:155. Fix: `.venv/bin/ruff format` on that file \u2014 the fence now also matches the formatting ruff already enforces on the source test file. Verified: `ruff format --check .` -> `153 files already formatted`, and `ruff check plugin/` -> `All checks passed!`. The other red lane (board ID validation) belongs to the existing row INT-CI-009, whose missing string evidence body + null created_by were the fatal violation; that row was backfilled with its real evidence in the same commit and stays pending because a real end-to-end bunker launch is not re-proven.", "description": "CI lint lane was red on main from dogfood commit 016adc1: `ruff format --check .` rejected the python fence in docs/dogfood/2026-10-20-composed-mode-egress-reporting.md (ruff formats markdown code fences). Fixed by formatting that file in commit 723ddd62cd2ec3d44f1cf509aa4363302298c08a (tick terminal-jail-foreman-2026-10-20-03-04-28). Exact-SHA evidence: local `ruff format --check .` = 153 files already formatted, `ruff check plugin/` = All checks passed; GitHub Actions run 39363383191 on 723ddd6 = all 6 jobs success (Python 3.11/3.12/3.13, Lint (ruff), Audit (pip-audit), Drift guards). No product code changed.", "detail": "failing step: 'Lint (ruff) :: Run ruff format check'; file: docs/dogfood/2026-10-20-composed-mode-egress-reporting.md:155; fix commit: 723ddd62cd2ec3d44f1cf509aa4363302298c08a", "evidence": "gh run view 39361059563 (1f830c5) -> Lint (ruff) failure step 'Run ruff format check'; local repro: .venv/bin/ruff format --check . -> 1 file would be reformatted; post-fix: ruff format --check . -> 153 files already formatted; ruff check plugin/ -> All checks passed!; gh run view 39363383191 @ 723ddd6 -> Python 3.11 success, Python 3.12 success, Python 3.13 success, Lint (ruff) success, Audit (pip-audit) success, Drift guards success"}
